      "kind": "list",
      "label": "1. The short version",
      "excerpt": "The risk is real, but narrow today. Across the 33 examples, two rules read the s",
      "text": "examples",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-21T01:13:38.663Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-21T01:55:14.424Z",
          "html": "<p>Each bullet in \"The short version\" now has an example under it: the Spell line, and what it really does.</p>\n<p>E.g. <code>red if it is a diamond or it is a heart</code> turns every heart black once a library has a heart; <code>para cada artículo en sus artículos</code> is a loop only by order; the jack, queen or king warning works with no agent.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-21T01:46:59.103Z"
      }
    },
    "c2": {
      "anchor": "dir-catching#code-1",
      "kind": "code",
      "label": "5.1 Catching double meanings",
      "excerpt": "What the person sees · adding Valentines to Solitaire Adding Valentines would ch",
      "text": "Your dialog is not worded at all clearly, but I get the idea.",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-21T01:35:10.533Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "edited": "2026-11-21T01:35:24.257Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-21T01:55:15.958Z",
          "html": "<p>The dialog in 5.1 is rewritten in the novice voice: it says what Valentines is, what its \"heart\" is, which 3 lines would switch and what each button does.</p>\n<p>The cold check (<code>epic voice check</code>) passed on the third draft. The first two failed on \"library\", two look-alike buttons and an unexplained \"keep them\".</p>"
        },
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "at": "2026-11-21T01:57:15.308Z",
          "text": "Better, but it could still be less verbose and clearer at the same time.  Bullets and newlines would help a lot.\nWe can add a phase to really tune this language.",
          "edited": "2026-11-21T01:59:54.861Z"
        },
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-21T02:09:32.227Z",
          "html": "<p>Noted:  a todo for a phase that tunes these words (T2), short lines and bullets, tuned with you.  Left as is on the page until then.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-21T01:47:00.467Z"
      }
    },
    "c3": {
      "anchor": "dir-explaining#code-1",
      "kind": "code",
      "label": "5.2 Explaining a line",
      "excerpt": "What the person sees · the hover's first line the card is the queen of spades Sp",
      "text": "This is gobbldegook and wrong\n\nUnderstood as:  \n- Make a new thing \"card\" in this action and set it to the existing thing \"queen of spades\".",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-21T01:36:16.487Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "edited": "2026-11-21T01:38:00.306Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-21T01:55:17.417Z",
          "html": "<p>You're right, and the facts were off too. I compiled it in a copy of Solitaire's card: <code>const card = \"spades\".queen</code>. There is no existing queen of spades. It's the queen of the word \"spades\", which is nothing, and every later <code>the card</code> in that action reads that empty name, not the card.</p>\n<p>The hover in 5.2 now says that first, \"This line doesn't check your card\", then why, then the line to write: <code>if it is the queen of spades</code>, checked to compile to <code>this.isTheRankOfSuit(\"queen\", \"spades\")</code>. Notes under it say what was checked.</p>"
        },
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "at": "2026-11-21T02:00:45.091Z",
          "text": "Again we'll tune this later,  Getting this right will be very important.",
          "edited": "2026-11-21T02:02:43.942Z"
        },
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-21T02:09:33.582Z",
          "html": "<p>Noted:  a todo for a phase that tunes these words (T2), short lines and bullets, tuned with you.  Left as is on the page until then.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-21T01:47:01.870Z"
      }
    },
    "c7": {
      "anchor": "words",
      "kind": "section",
      "label": "8. Words",
